---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You have a ticket, a record, or a log, and you need answers your code can branch on.\nA queue name. An urgency level. A yes or no.\nBy the end of this guide you call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"decide()"},{"type":"text","value":" once and read typed fields like "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"result.queue.value"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"decide()"},{"type":"text","value":" takes an adapter, a state, and a map of questions. There is no stream."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"providers","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Providers"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Evaluate talks to a decision model through six adapters:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/ollaya","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ollaya"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-ollaya"},{"type":"text","value":"): "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ollayaDecider('laya:latest')"},{"type":"text","value":". Local server at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"http://127.0.0.1:11435"},{"type":"text","value":". No API key."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TypeSafe"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-typesafe"},{"type":"text","value":"): "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"typesafeDecider('jev-latest')"},{"type":"text","value":". Reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TYPESAFE_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenRouter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-openrouter"},{"type":"text","value":"): "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openRouterDecider('~typesafe/jev-latest')"},{"type":"text","value":". Reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENROUTER_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vercel AI Gateway"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-vercel-gateway"},{"type":"text","value":"): "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"vercelGatewayDecider('typesafe-ai/jev')"},{"type":"text","value":". Reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cloudflare"}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-cloudflare"},{"type":"text","value":"): "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"cloudflareDecider('typesafe/jev')"},{"type":"text","value":". Uses a Worker binding, or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/openai#evaluate","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI"}]}]},{"type":"text","value":" ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-openai"},{"type":"text","value":"): "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openaiDecider('gpt-6-luna')"},{"type":"text","value":". Reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENAI_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"All six implement the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"evaluate"},{"type":"text","value":" activity. Swap the adapter. Keep the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"decide()"},{"type":"text","value":" call."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"installation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Installation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TypeSafe:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-typesafe\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-typesafe\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-typesafe\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-typesafe\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-typesafe\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-typesafe\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-typesafe\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai-typesafe\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Peer dependency:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"vue\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"solid\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"svelte\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"preact\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"angular\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"vanilla\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\"]],\"octane\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Other adapters:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/ollaya","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ollaya"}]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-ollaya"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenRouter: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-openrouter"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vercel AI Gateway: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-vercel-gateway"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cloudflare: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-cloudflare"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/openai#evaluate","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenAI"}]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-openai"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"basic-usage","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Basic Usage"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"decide()"},{"type":"text","value":" with an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"adapter"},{"type":"text","value":", a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":", and a map of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"questions"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { decide, choice, score, boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { typesafeDecider } from '@tanstack/ai-typesafe'\n\nconst ticket = {\n  subject: 'Charged twice for the same invoice',\n  body: 'Please refund the extra payment.',\n}\n\nconst result = await decide({\n  adapter: typesafeDecider('jev-latest'),\n  state: ticket,\n  questions: {\n    queue: choice({\n      instructions: 'Which team should handle this ticket?',\n      options: {\n        billing: 'Payments, invoices, refunds',\n        tech: 'Bugs, outages, integrations',\n        sales: 'Pricing, upgrades, new accounts',\n      },\n    }),\n    urgency: score({\n      instructions: 'How urgent is this ticket?',\n      levels: ['low', 'medium', 'high'],\n    }),\n    refund: boolean({\n      instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n    }),\n  },\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.queue.value)\nconsole.log(result.queue.probability)\nconsole.log(result.queue.confidence)\nconsole.log(result.meta.usage)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"decide()"},{"type":"text","value":" is async. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"typesafeDecider"},{"type":"text","value":" reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TYPESAFE_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" from the environment.\nTo pass a key yourself, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createTypesafeDecider('jev-latest', 'ts-...')"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To evaluate through OpenRouter, swap the adapter. Everything else stays the same:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { decide, choice, score, boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openRouterDecider } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter'\n\nconst ticket = {\n  subject: 'Charged twice for the same invoice',\n  body: 'Please refund the extra payment.',\n}\n\nconst result = await decide({\n  adapter: openRouterDecider('~typesafe/jev-latest'),\n  state: ticket,\n  questions: {\n    queue: choice({\n      instructions: 'Which team should handle this ticket?',\n      options: {\n        billing: 'Payments, invoices, refunds',\n        tech: 'Bugs, outages, integrations',\n        sales: 'Pricing, upgrades, new accounts',\n      },\n    }),\n    urgency: score({\n      instructions: 'How urgent is this ticket?',\n      levels: ['low', 'medium', 'high'],\n    }),\n    refund: boolean({\n      instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n    }),\n  },\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.queue.value)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"openRouterDecider"},{"type":"text","value":" reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENROUTER_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" from the environment."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"questions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Questions"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass a map of questions. Each key becomes a property on the result.\nThe key "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"meta"},{"type":"text","value":" is reserved."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"instructions"},{"type":"text","value":" can be a string, an object, or an array.\nAn array is one state, not a batch."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"choice","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"choice()"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The model picks one key from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"options"},{"type":"text","value":". Option keys become the union on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".value"},{"type":"text","value":".\nWhen a key needs no extra description, use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { choice } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nconst queue = choice({\n  instructions: 'Which team should handle this ticket?',\n  options: {\n    billing: 'Payments, invoices, refunds',\n    tech: 'Bugs, outages, integrations',\n    sales: 'Pricing, upgrades, new accounts',\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"score","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"score()"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The model rates "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":" on ordered "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"levels"},{"type":"text","value":". You must pass at least two levels.\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".value"},{"type":"text","value":" is the nearest level label. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".score"},{"type":"text","value":" is the raw fraction."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { score } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nconst urgency = score({\n  instructions: 'How urgent is this ticket?',\n  levels: ['low', 'medium', 'high'],\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"boolean","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean()"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A yes or no question. When "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"probability"},{"type":"text","value":" is 0.5 or more, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".value"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":".\nThere is no "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".confidence"},{"type":"text","value":". On the TypeSafe wire, this type is named "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"noul"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nconst refund = boolean({\n  instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n})","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"criteria: { true: '...', false: '...' }"},{"type":"text","value":" to describe each side."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"result-shape","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result Shape"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each question key is a top-level answer. Usage and the resolved model sit on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"meta"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { decide, choice, score, boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { typesafeDecider } from '@tanstack/ai-typesafe'\n\nconst result = await decide({\n  adapter: typesafeDecider('jev-latest'),\n  state: 'Please refund the extra payment.',\n  questions: {\n    queue: choice({\n      instructions: 'Which team should handle this ticket?',\n      options: {\n        billing: 'Payments, invoices, refunds',\n        tech: 'Bugs, outages, integrations',\n      },\n    }),\n    urgency: score({\n      instructions: 'How urgent is this ticket?',\n      levels: ['low', 'medium', 'high'],\n    }),\n    refund: boolean({\n      instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n    }),\n  },\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.queue.value)\nconsole.log(result.queue.probability)\nconsole.log(result.queue.confidence)\nconsole.log(result.queue.probabilities)\n\nconsole.log(result.urgency.value)\nconsole.log(result.urgency.score)\nconsole.log(result.urgency.probability)\nconsole.log(result.urgency.confidence)\nconsole.log(result.urgency.legend)\nconsole.log(result.urgency.probabilities)\n\nconsole.log(result.refund.value)\nconsole.log(result.refund.probability)\n\nconsole.log(result.meta.model)\nconsole.log(result.meta.usage)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"choice"}]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".value"},{"type":"text","value":" is the selected option key. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".probability"},{"type":"text","value":" is P(selected). "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".probabilities"},{"type":"text","value":" is the full map."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"score"}]},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".value"},{"type":"text","value":" is the nearest level. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".score"},{"type":"text","value":" is the raw fraction. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".probability"},{"type":"text","value":" is P(that level). "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".legend"},{"type":"text","value":" maps each level index to its label. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".probabilities"},{"type":"text","value":" is the full map, keyed by level index."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"boolean"}]},{"type":"text","value":": When P(true) is 0.5 or more, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".value"},{"type":"text","value":" is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"true"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".probability"},{"type":"text","value":" is P(true). No "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".confidence"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Options"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"decide","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"decide()"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Option"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Description"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"adapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"EvaluateAdapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An evaluate adapter created with a model (required)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"string | object | array"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Shared content every question judges (required)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"questions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Record<string, Question>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Map of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"choice"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"score"},{"type":"text","value":", and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"boolean"},{"type":"text","value":" questions (required)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"abortSignal"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AbortSignal"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cancel the in-flight request"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"modelOptions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"provider options"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provider-specific options"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"middleware"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Array<GenerationMiddleware>"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Observe-only lifecycle hooks (usage, finish, error, abort)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"debug"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"DebugOption"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Debug logging"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"server-endpoint","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server Endpoint"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Evaluate runs on the server. The call needs your API key. Wrap it in an API\nroute. Call it from the client over "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetch"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// routes/api/evaluate.ts\nimport { decide, choice, score, boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { typesafeDecider } from '@tanstack/ai-typesafe'\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst ADAPTER = typesafeDecider('jev-latest')\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/evaluate')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST: async ({ request }) => {\n        const body: unknown = await request.json()\n        if (\n          typeof body !== 'object' ||\n          body === null ||\n          !('ticket' in body)\n        ) {\n          return new Response('Invalid request body', { status: 400 })\n        }\n        const { ticket } = body\n\n        const result = await decide({\n          adapter: ADAPTER,\n          state: ticket,\n          questions: {\n            queue: choice({\n              instructions: 'Which team should handle this ticket?',\n              options: {\n                billing: 'Payments, invoices, refunds',\n                tech: 'Bugs, outages, integrations',\n                sales: 'Pricing, upgrades, new accounts',\n              },\n            }),\n            urgency: score({\n              instructions: 'How urgent is this ticket?',\n              levels: ['low', 'medium', 'high'],\n            }),\n            refund: boolean({\n              instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n            }),\n          },\n        })\n\n        return Response.json(result)\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"code","value":"// client.ts\nasync function evaluateTicket(ticket: { subject: string; body: string }) {\n  const res = await fetch('/api/evaluate', {\n    method: 'POST',\n    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    body: JSON.stringify({ ticket }),\n  })\n  return res.json()\n}","lang":"typescript","meta":"ignore"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"cancellation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cancellation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass an "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"abortSignal"},{"type":"text","value":" to cancel an in-flight request:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { decide, boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { typesafeDecider } from '@tanstack/ai-typesafe'\n\nconst controller = new AbortController()\nsetTimeout(() => controller.abort(), 5000)\n\nconst result = await decide({\n  adapter: typesafeDecider('jev-latest'),\n  state: 'Please refund the extra payment.',\n  questions: {\n    refund: boolean({\n      instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n    }),\n  },\n  abortSignal: controller.signal,\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.refund.value)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"observability","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Observability"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Attach observe-only middleware to track usage, completion, errors, and\ncancellation. This is the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"GenerationMiddleware"},{"type":"text","value":" contract the media\nactivities use:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { decide, boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { typesafeDecider } from '@tanstack/ai-typesafe'\n\nconst result = await decide({\n  adapter: typesafeDecider('jev-latest'),\n  state: 'Please refund the extra payment.',\n  questions: {\n    refund: boolean({\n      instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n    }),\n  },\n  middleware: [\n    {\n      name: 'usage-logger',\n      onUsage: (_ctx, usage) => {\n        console.log(`prompt tokens: ${usage.promptTokens}`)\n      },\n    },\n  ],\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.refund.value)","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tip:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" Pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"otelMiddleware()"},{"type":"text","value":" to emit OpenTelemetry spans for evaluate\ncalls. See "},{"type":"link","href":"../advanced/otel","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenTelemetry"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"environment-variables","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Environment Variables"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Each adapter reads its own key:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TypeSafe: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TYPESAFE_API_KEY"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenRouter: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENROUTER_API_KEY"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vercel AI Gateway: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" (or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN"},{"type":"text","value":")"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cloudflare REST: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You only need the key for the adapter you pick."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"error-handling","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Error Handling"}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { decide, boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { typesafeDecider } from '@tanstack/ai-typesafe'\n\ntry {\n  const result = await decide({\n    adapter: typesafeDecider('jev-latest'),\n    state: 'Please refund the extra payment.',\n    questions: {\n      refund: boolean({\n        instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n      }),\n    },\n  })\n  console.log(result.refund.value)\n} catch (error) {\n  if (error instanceof Error) {\n    console.error('Evaluate failed:', error.message)\n  }\n}","lang":"typescript"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"questions"},{"type":"text","value":" is empty, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"decide()"},{"type":"text","value":" throws before any request.\nIf a question key is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"meta"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"decide()"},{"type":"text","value":" throws."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"runnable-example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runnable Example"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/react/evaluate"},{"type":"text","value":" is a small TanStack Start app that runs this page.\nPaste a support ticket. The UI shows queue, urgency, and refund.\nThe dropdown lists five adapters. Each call to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"decide()"},{"type":"text","value":" uses the same questions."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Copy "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".env.example"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".env"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you pick a hosted adapter, add its key in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":".env"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you pick Ollaya, run "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ollaya serve"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you pick Ollaya, run "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ollaya pull laya:latest"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run the dev server with the command below."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ollaya does not need an API key."}]},{"type":"code","value":"pnpm --filter evaluate dev","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Open http://localhost:3100."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next-steps","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next Steps"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Local:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/ollaya","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ollaya Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Local "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"laya"},{"type":"text","value":" decisions. No API key."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/typesafe","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TypeSafe Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Direct Jev, models, and explicit API keys"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../tutorials/evaluate","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Evaluate a ticket"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Build a Start route that routes a ticket"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hosted:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/openrouter","children":[{"type":"text","value":"OpenRouter Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Evaluate through your OpenRouter key"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/vercel-gateway","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vercel AI Gateway"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Evaluate through the Gateway"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../adapters/cloudflare","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cloudflare Adapter"}]},{"type":"text","value":" - Evaluate from a Worker or REST"}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"providers","text":"Providers","level":2},{"id":"installation","text":"Installation","level":2},{"id":"basic-usage","text":"Basic Usage","level":2},{"id":"questions","text":"Questions","level":2},{"id":"choice","text":"choice()","level":3},{"id":"score","text":"score()","level":3},{"id":"boolean","text":"boolean()","level":3},{"id":"result-shape","text":"Result Shape","level":2},{"id":"options","text":"Options","level":2},{"id":"decide","text":"decide()","level":3},{"id":"server-endpoint","text":"Server Endpoint","level":2},{"id":"cancellation","text":"Cancellation","level":2},{"id":"observability","text":"Observability","level":2},{"id":"environment-variables","text":"Environment Variables","level":2},{"id":"error-handling","text":"Error Handling","level":2},{"id":"runnable-example","text":"Runnable Example","level":2},{"id":"next-steps","text":"Next Steps","level":2}]},"frameworks":["react","vue","solid","svelte","preact","angular","vanilla","octane"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou have a ticket, a record, or a log, and you need answers your code can branch on.\nA queue name. An urgency level. A yes or no.\nBy the end of this guide you call `decide()` once and read typed fields like `result.queue.value`.\n\n`decide()` takes an adapter, a state, and a map of questions. There is no stream.\n\n## Providers\n\nEvaluate talks to a decision model through six adapters:\n\n- **[Ollaya](../adapters/ollaya)** (`@tanstack/ai-ollaya`): `ollayaDecider('laya:latest')`. Local server at `http://127.0.0.1:11435`. No API key.\n- **TypeSafe** (`@tanstack/ai-typesafe`): `typesafeDecider('jev-latest')`. Reads `TYPESAFE_API_KEY`.\n- **OpenRouter** (`@tanstack/ai-openrouter`): `openRouterDecider('~typesafe/jev-latest')`. Reads `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`.\n- **Vercel AI Gateway** (`@tanstack/ai-vercel-gateway`): `vercelGatewayDecider('typesafe-ai/jev')`. Reads `AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY`.\n- **Cloudflare** (`@tanstack/ai-cloudflare`): `cloudflareDecider('typesafe/jev')`. Uses a Worker binding, or `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` and `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`.\n- **[OpenAI](../adapters/openai#evaluate)** (`@tanstack/ai-openai`): `openaiDecider('gpt-6-luna')`. Reads `OPENAI_API_KEY`.\n\nAll six implement the same `evaluate` activity. Swap the adapter. Keep the `decide()` call.\n\n## Installation\n\nTypeSafe:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-typesafe\nvue: @tanstack/ai-typesafe\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-typesafe\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-typesafe\npreact: @tanstack/ai-typesafe\nangular: @tanstack/ai-typesafe\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-typesafe\noctane: @tanstack/ai-typesafe\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nPeer dependency:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai\nvue: @tanstack/ai\nsolid: @tanstack/ai\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai\npreact: @tanstack/ai\nangular: @tanstack/ai\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai\noctane: @tanstack/ai\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nOther adapters:\n\n- [Ollaya](../adapters/ollaya): `@tanstack/ai-ollaya`\n- OpenRouter: `@tanstack/ai-openrouter`\n- Vercel AI Gateway: `@tanstack/ai-vercel-gateway`\n- Cloudflare: `@tanstack/ai-cloudflare`\n- [OpenAI](../adapters/openai#evaluate): `@tanstack/ai-openai`\n\n## Basic Usage\n\nCall `decide()` with an `adapter`, a `state`, and a map of `questions`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { decide, choice, score, boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { typesafeDecider } from '@tanstack/ai-typesafe'\n\nconst ticket = {\n  subject: 'Charged twice for the same invoice',\n  body: 'Please refund the extra payment.',\n}\n\nconst result = await decide({\n  adapter: typesafeDecider('jev-latest'),\n  state: ticket,\n  questions: {\n    queue: choice({\n      instructions: 'Which team should handle this ticket?',\n      options: {\n        billing: 'Payments, invoices, refunds',\n        tech: 'Bugs, outages, integrations',\n        sales: 'Pricing, upgrades, new accounts',\n      },\n    }),\n    urgency: score({\n      instructions: 'How urgent is this ticket?',\n      levels: ['low', 'medium', 'high'],\n    }),\n    refund: boolean({\n      instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n    }),\n  },\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.queue.value)\nconsole.log(result.queue.probability)\nconsole.log(result.queue.confidence)\nconsole.log(result.meta.usage)\n```\n\n`decide()` is async. `typesafeDecider` reads `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` from the environment.\nTo pass a key yourself, use `createTypesafeDecider('jev-latest', 'ts-...')`.\n\nTo evaluate through OpenRouter, swap the adapter. Everything else stays the same:\n\n```typescript\nimport { decide, choice, score, boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openRouterDecider } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter'\n\nconst ticket = {\n  subject: 'Charged twice for the same invoice',\n  body: 'Please refund the extra payment.',\n}\n\nconst result = await decide({\n  adapter: openRouterDecider('~typesafe/jev-latest'),\n  state: ticket,\n  questions: {\n    queue: choice({\n      instructions: 'Which team should handle this ticket?',\n      options: {\n        billing: 'Payments, invoices, refunds',\n        tech: 'Bugs, outages, integrations',\n        sales: 'Pricing, upgrades, new accounts',\n      },\n    }),\n    urgency: score({\n      instructions: 'How urgent is this ticket?',\n      levels: ['low', 'medium', 'high'],\n    }),\n    refund: boolean({\n      instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n    }),\n  },\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.queue.value)\n```\n\n`openRouterDecider` reads `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` from the environment.\n\n## Questions\n\nPass a map of questions. Each key becomes a property on the result.\nThe key `meta` is reserved.\n\n`state` and `instructions` can be a string, an object, or an array.\nAn array is one state, not a batch.\n\n### `choice()`\n\nThe model picks one key from `options`. Option keys become the union on `.value`.\nWhen a key needs no extra description, use `null`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { choice } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nconst queue = choice({\n  instructions: 'Which team should handle this ticket?',\n  options: {\n    billing: 'Payments, invoices, refunds',\n    tech: 'Bugs, outages, integrations',\n    sales: 'Pricing, upgrades, new accounts',\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### `score()`\n\nThe model rates `state` on ordered `levels`. You must pass at least two levels.\n`.value` is the nearest level label. `.score` is the raw fraction.\n\n```typescript\nimport { score } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nconst urgency = score({\n  instructions: 'How urgent is this ticket?',\n  levels: ['low', 'medium', 'high'],\n})\n```\n\n### `boolean()`\n\nA yes or no question. When `probability` is 0.5 or more, `.value` is `true`.\nThere is no `.confidence`. On the TypeSafe wire, this type is named `noul`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nconst refund = boolean({\n  instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n})\n```\n\nYou can pass `criteria: { true: '...', false: '...' }` to describe each side.\n\n## Result Shape\n\nEach question key is a top-level answer. Usage and the resolved model sit on `meta`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { decide, choice, score, boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { typesafeDecider } from '@tanstack/ai-typesafe'\n\nconst result = await decide({\n  adapter: typesafeDecider('jev-latest'),\n  state: 'Please refund the extra payment.',\n  questions: {\n    queue: choice({\n      instructions: 'Which team should handle this ticket?',\n      options: {\n        billing: 'Payments, invoices, refunds',\n        tech: 'Bugs, outages, integrations',\n      },\n    }),\n    urgency: score({\n      instructions: 'How urgent is this ticket?',\n      levels: ['low', 'medium', 'high'],\n    }),\n    refund: boolean({\n      instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n    }),\n  },\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.queue.value)\nconsole.log(result.queue.probability)\nconsole.log(result.queue.confidence)\nconsole.log(result.queue.probabilities)\n\nconsole.log(result.urgency.value)\nconsole.log(result.urgency.score)\nconsole.log(result.urgency.probability)\nconsole.log(result.urgency.confidence)\nconsole.log(result.urgency.legend)\nconsole.log(result.urgency.probabilities)\n\nconsole.log(result.refund.value)\nconsole.log(result.refund.probability)\n\nconsole.log(result.meta.model)\nconsole.log(result.meta.usage)\n```\n\n- **choice**: `.value` is the selected option key. `.probability` is P(selected). `.probabilities` is the full map.\n- **score**: `.value` is the nearest level. `.score` is the raw fraction. `.probability` is P(that level). `.legend` maps each level index to its label. `.probabilities` is the full map, keyed by level index.\n- **boolean**: When P(true) is 0.5 or more, `.value` is `true`. `.probability` is P(true). No `.confidence`.\n\n## Options\n\n### `decide()`\n\n| Option         | Type                          | Description                                                  |\n| -------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `adapter`      | `EvaluateAdapter`             | An evaluate adapter created with a model (required)          |\n| `state`        | `string \\| object \\| array`   | Shared content every question judges (required)              |\n| `questions`    | `Record<string, Question>`    | Map of `choice`, `score`, and `boolean` questions (required) |\n| `abortSignal`  | `AbortSignal`                 | Cancel the in-flight request                                 |\n| `modelOptions` | provider options              | Provider-specific options                                    |\n| `middleware`   | `Array<GenerationMiddleware>` | Observe-only lifecycle hooks (usage, finish, error, abort)   |\n| `debug`        | `DebugOption`                 | Debug logging                                                |\n\n## Server Endpoint\n\nEvaluate runs on the server. The call needs your API key. Wrap it in an API\nroute. Call it from the client over `fetch`:\n\n```typescript ignore\n// routes/api/evaluate.ts\nimport { decide, choice, score, boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { typesafeDecider } from '@tanstack/ai-typesafe'\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst ADAPTER = typesafeDecider('jev-latest')\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/evaluate')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST: async ({ request }) => {\n        const body: unknown = await request.json()\n        if (\n          typeof body !== 'object' ||\n          body === null ||\n          !('ticket' in body)\n        ) {\n          return new Response('Invalid request body', { status: 400 })\n        }\n        const { ticket } = body\n\n        const result = await decide({\n          adapter: ADAPTER,\n          state: ticket,\n          questions: {\n            queue: choice({\n              instructions: 'Which team should handle this ticket?',\n              options: {\n                billing: 'Payments, invoices, refunds',\n                tech: 'Bugs, outages, integrations',\n                sales: 'Pricing, upgrades, new accounts',\n              },\n            }),\n            urgency: score({\n              instructions: 'How urgent is this ticket?',\n              levels: ['low', 'medium', 'high'],\n            }),\n            refund: boolean({\n              instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n            }),\n          },\n        })\n\n        return Response.json(result)\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n```typescript ignore\n// client.ts\nasync function evaluateTicket(ticket: { subject: string; body: string }) {\n  const res = await fetch('/api/evaluate', {\n    method: 'POST',\n    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    body: JSON.stringify({ ticket }),\n  })\n  return res.json()\n}\n```\n\n## Cancellation\n\nPass an `abortSignal` to cancel an in-flight request:\n\n```typescript\nimport { decide, boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { typesafeDecider } from '@tanstack/ai-typesafe'\n\nconst controller = new AbortController()\nsetTimeout(() => controller.abort(), 5000)\n\nconst result = await decide({\n  adapter: typesafeDecider('jev-latest'),\n  state: 'Please refund the extra payment.',\n  questions: {\n    refund: boolean({\n      instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n    }),\n  },\n  abortSignal: controller.signal,\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.refund.value)\n```\n\n## Observability\n\nAttach observe-only middleware to track usage, completion, errors, and\ncancellation. This is the same `GenerationMiddleware` contract the media\nactivities use:\n\n```typescript\nimport { decide, boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { typesafeDecider } from '@tanstack/ai-typesafe'\n\nconst result = await decide({\n  adapter: typesafeDecider('jev-latest'),\n  state: 'Please refund the extra payment.',\n  questions: {\n    refund: boolean({\n      instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n    }),\n  },\n  middleware: [\n    {\n      name: 'usage-logger',\n      onUsage: (_ctx, usage) => {\n        console.log(`prompt tokens: ${usage.promptTokens}`)\n      },\n    },\n  ],\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.refund.value)\n```\n\n> **Tip:** Pass `otelMiddleware()` to emit OpenTelemetry spans for evaluate\n> calls. See [OpenTelemetry](../advanced/otel).\n\n## Environment Variables\n\nEach adapter reads its own key:\n\n- TypeSafe: `TYPESAFE_API_KEY`\n- OpenRouter: `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`\n- Vercel AI Gateway: `AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY` (or `VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN`)\n- Cloudflare REST: `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` and `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`\n\nYou only need the key for the adapter you pick.\n\n## Error Handling\n\n```typescript\nimport { decide, boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { typesafeDecider } from '@tanstack/ai-typesafe'\n\ntry {\n  const result = await decide({\n    adapter: typesafeDecider('jev-latest'),\n    state: 'Please refund the extra payment.',\n    questions: {\n      refund: boolean({\n        instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n      }),\n    },\n  })\n  console.log(result.refund.value)\n} catch (error) {\n  if (error instanceof Error) {\n    console.error('Evaluate failed:', error.message)\n  }\n}\n```\n\nIf `questions` is empty, `decide()` throws before any request.\nIf a question key is `meta`, `decide()` throws.\n\n## Runnable Example\n\n`examples/react/evaluate` is a small TanStack Start app that runs this page.\nPaste a support ticket. The UI shows queue, urgency, and refund.\nThe dropdown lists five adapters. Each call to `decide()` uses the same questions.\n\n1. Copy `.env.example` to `.env`.\n2. If you pick a hosted adapter, add its key in `.env`.\n3. If you pick Ollaya, run `ollaya serve`.\n4. If you pick Ollaya, run `ollaya pull laya:latest`.\n5. Run the dev server with the command below.\n\nOllaya does not need an API key.\n\n```bash\npnpm --filter evaluate dev\n```\n\nOpen http://localhost:3100.\n\n## Next Steps\n\nLocal:\n\n- [Ollaya Adapter](../adapters/ollaya) - Local `laya` decisions. No API key.\n- [TypeSafe Adapter](../adapters/typesafe) - Direct Jev, models, and explicit API keys\n- [Evaluate a ticket](../tutorials/evaluate) - Build a Start route that routes a ticket\n\nHosted:\n\n- [OpenRouter Adapter](../adapters/openrouter) - Evaluate through your OpenRouter key\n- [Vercel AI Gateway](../adapters/vercel-gateway) - Evaluate through the Gateway\n- [Cloudflare Adapter](../adapters/cloudflare) - Evaluate from a Worker or REST\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Evaluate\nid: evaluate\norder: 1\ndescription: \"Ask typed choice, score, and boolean questions about shared state with decide().\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - evaluate\n  - decide\n  - typed decisions\n  - choice\n  - score\n  - boolean\n  - typesafe\n  - jev\n  - ollaya\n  - laya\n---\n\nYou have a ticket, a record, or a log, and you need answers your code can branch on.\nA queue name. An urgency level. A yes or no.\nBy the end of this guide you call `decide()` once and read typed fields like `result.queue.value`.\n\n`decide()` takes an adapter, a state, and a map of questions. There is no stream.\n\n## Providers\n\nEvaluate talks to a decision model through six adapters:\n\n- **[Ollaya](../adapters/ollaya)** (`@tanstack/ai-ollaya`): `ollayaDecider('laya:latest')`. Local server at `http://127.0.0.1:11435`. No API key.\n- **TypeSafe** (`@tanstack/ai-typesafe`): `typesafeDecider('jev-latest')`. Reads `TYPESAFE_API_KEY`.\n- **OpenRouter** (`@tanstack/ai-openrouter`): `openRouterDecider('~typesafe/jev-latest')`. Reads `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`.\n- **Vercel AI Gateway** (`@tanstack/ai-vercel-gateway`): `vercelGatewayDecider('typesafe-ai/jev')`. Reads `AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY`.\n- **Cloudflare** (`@tanstack/ai-cloudflare`): `cloudflareDecider('typesafe/jev')`. Uses a Worker binding, or `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` and `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`.\n- **[OpenAI](../adapters/openai#evaluate)** (`@tanstack/ai-openai`): `openaiDecider('gpt-6-luna')`. Reads `OPENAI_API_KEY`.\n\nAll six implement the same `evaluate` activity. Swap the adapter. Keep the `decide()` call.\n\n## Installation\n\nTypeSafe:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai-typesafe\nvue: @tanstack/ai-typesafe\nsolid: @tanstack/ai-typesafe\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai-typesafe\npreact: @tanstack/ai-typesafe\nangular: @tanstack/ai-typesafe\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai-typesafe\noctane: @tanstack/ai-typesafe\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nPeer dependency:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai\nvue: @tanstack/ai\nsolid: @tanstack/ai\nsvelte: @tanstack/ai\npreact: @tanstack/ai\nangular: @tanstack/ai\nvanilla: @tanstack/ai\noctane: @tanstack/ai\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nOther adapters:\n\n- [Ollaya](../adapters/ollaya): `@tanstack/ai-ollaya`\n- OpenRouter: `@tanstack/ai-openrouter`\n- Vercel AI Gateway: `@tanstack/ai-vercel-gateway`\n- Cloudflare: `@tanstack/ai-cloudflare`\n- [OpenAI](../adapters/openai#evaluate): `@tanstack/ai-openai`\n\n## Basic Usage\n\nCall `decide()` with an `adapter`, a `state`, and a map of `questions`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { decide, choice, score, boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { typesafeDecider } from '@tanstack/ai-typesafe'\n\nconst ticket = {\n  subject: 'Charged twice for the same invoice',\n  body: 'Please refund the extra payment.',\n}\n\nconst result = await decide({\n  adapter: typesafeDecider('jev-latest'),\n  state: ticket,\n  questions: {\n    queue: choice({\n      instructions: 'Which team should handle this ticket?',\n      options: {\n        billing: 'Payments, invoices, refunds',\n        tech: 'Bugs, outages, integrations',\n        sales: 'Pricing, upgrades, new accounts',\n      },\n    }),\n    urgency: score({\n      instructions: 'How urgent is this ticket?',\n      levels: ['low', 'medium', 'high'],\n    }),\n    refund: boolean({\n      instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n    }),\n  },\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.queue.value)\nconsole.log(result.queue.probability)\nconsole.log(result.queue.confidence)\nconsole.log(result.meta.usage)\n```\n\n`decide()` is async. `typesafeDecider` reads `TYPESAFE_API_KEY` from the environment.\nTo pass a key yourself, use `createTypesafeDecider('jev-latest', 'ts-...')`.\n\nTo evaluate through OpenRouter, swap the adapter. Everything else stays the same:\n\n```typescript\nimport { decide, choice, score, boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openRouterDecider } from '@tanstack/ai-openrouter'\n\nconst ticket = {\n  subject: 'Charged twice for the same invoice',\n  body: 'Please refund the extra payment.',\n}\n\nconst result = await decide({\n  adapter: openRouterDecider('~typesafe/jev-latest'),\n  state: ticket,\n  questions: {\n    queue: choice({\n      instructions: 'Which team should handle this ticket?',\n      options: {\n        billing: 'Payments, invoices, refunds',\n        tech: 'Bugs, outages, integrations',\n        sales: 'Pricing, upgrades, new accounts',\n      },\n    }),\n    urgency: score({\n      instructions: 'How urgent is this ticket?',\n      levels: ['low', 'medium', 'high'],\n    }),\n    refund: boolean({\n      instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n    }),\n  },\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.queue.value)\n```\n\n`openRouterDecider` reads `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` from the environment.\n\n## Questions\n\nPass a map of questions. Each key becomes a property on the result.\nThe key `meta` is reserved.\n\n`state` and `instructions` can be a string, an object, or an array.\nAn array is one state, not a batch.\n\n### `choice()`\n\nThe model picks one key from `options`. Option keys become the union on `.value`.\nWhen a key needs no extra description, use `null`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { choice } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nconst queue = choice({\n  instructions: 'Which team should handle this ticket?',\n  options: {\n    billing: 'Payments, invoices, refunds',\n    tech: 'Bugs, outages, integrations',\n    sales: 'Pricing, upgrades, new accounts',\n  },\n})\n```\n\n### `score()`\n\nThe model rates `state` on ordered `levels`. You must pass at least two levels.\n`.value` is the nearest level label. `.score` is the raw fraction.\n\n```typescript\nimport { score } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nconst urgency = score({\n  instructions: 'How urgent is this ticket?',\n  levels: ['low', 'medium', 'high'],\n})\n```\n\n### `boolean()`\n\nA yes or no question. When `probability` is 0.5 or more, `.value` is `true`.\nThere is no `.confidence`. On the TypeSafe wire, this type is named `noul`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\n\nconst refund = boolean({\n  instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n})\n```\n\nYou can pass `criteria: { true: '...', false: '...' }` to describe each side.\n\n## Result Shape\n\nEach question key is a top-level answer. Usage and the resolved model sit on `meta`.\n\n```typescript\nimport { decide, choice, score, boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { typesafeDecider } from '@tanstack/ai-typesafe'\n\nconst result = await decide({\n  adapter: typesafeDecider('jev-latest'),\n  state: 'Please refund the extra payment.',\n  questions: {\n    queue: choice({\n      instructions: 'Which team should handle this ticket?',\n      options: {\n        billing: 'Payments, invoices, refunds',\n        tech: 'Bugs, outages, integrations',\n      },\n    }),\n    urgency: score({\n      instructions: 'How urgent is this ticket?',\n      levels: ['low', 'medium', 'high'],\n    }),\n    refund: boolean({\n      instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n    }),\n  },\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.queue.value)\nconsole.log(result.queue.probability)\nconsole.log(result.queue.confidence)\nconsole.log(result.queue.probabilities)\n\nconsole.log(result.urgency.value)\nconsole.log(result.urgency.score)\nconsole.log(result.urgency.probability)\nconsole.log(result.urgency.confidence)\nconsole.log(result.urgency.legend)\nconsole.log(result.urgency.probabilities)\n\nconsole.log(result.refund.value)\nconsole.log(result.refund.probability)\n\nconsole.log(result.meta.model)\nconsole.log(result.meta.usage)\n```\n\n- **choice**: `.value` is the selected option key. `.probability` is P(selected). `.probabilities` is the full map.\n- **score**: `.value` is the nearest level. `.score` is the raw fraction. `.probability` is P(that level). `.legend` maps each level index to its label. `.probabilities` is the full map, keyed by level index.\n- **boolean**: When P(true) is 0.5 or more, `.value` is `true`. `.probability` is P(true). No `.confidence`.\n\n## Options\n\n### `decide()`\n\n| Option         | Type                          | Description                                                  |\n| -------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `adapter`      | `EvaluateAdapter`             | An evaluate adapter created with a model (required)          |\n| `state`        | `string \\| object \\| array`   | Shared content every question judges (required)              |\n| `questions`    | `Record<string, Question>`    | Map of `choice`, `score`, and `boolean` questions (required) |\n| `abortSignal`  | `AbortSignal`                 | Cancel the in-flight request                                 |\n| `modelOptions` | provider options              | Provider-specific options                                    |\n| `middleware`   | `Array<GenerationMiddleware>` | Observe-only lifecycle hooks (usage, finish, error, abort)   |\n| `debug`        | `DebugOption`                 | Debug logging                                                |\n\n## Server Endpoint\n\nEvaluate runs on the server. The call needs your API key. Wrap it in an API\nroute. Call it from the client over `fetch`:\n\n```typescript ignore\n// routes/api/evaluate.ts\nimport { decide, choice, score, boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { typesafeDecider } from '@tanstack/ai-typesafe'\nimport { createFileRoute } from '@tanstack/react-router'\n\nconst ADAPTER = typesafeDecider('jev-latest')\n\nexport const Route = createFileRoute('/api/evaluate')({\n  server: {\n    handlers: {\n      POST: async ({ request }) => {\n        const body: unknown = await request.json()\n        if (\n          typeof body !== 'object' ||\n          body === null ||\n          !('ticket' in body)\n        ) {\n          return new Response('Invalid request body', { status: 400 })\n        }\n        const { ticket } = body\n\n        const result = await decide({\n          adapter: ADAPTER,\n          state: ticket,\n          questions: {\n            queue: choice({\n              instructions: 'Which team should handle this ticket?',\n              options: {\n                billing: 'Payments, invoices, refunds',\n                tech: 'Bugs, outages, integrations',\n                sales: 'Pricing, upgrades, new accounts',\n              },\n            }),\n            urgency: score({\n              instructions: 'How urgent is this ticket?',\n              levels: ['low', 'medium', 'high'],\n            }),\n            refund: boolean({\n              instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n            }),\n          },\n        })\n\n        return Response.json(result)\n      },\n    },\n  },\n})\n```\n\n```typescript ignore\n// client.ts\nasync function evaluateTicket(ticket: { subject: string; body: string }) {\n  const res = await fetch('/api/evaluate', {\n    method: 'POST',\n    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },\n    body: JSON.stringify({ ticket }),\n  })\n  return res.json()\n}\n```\n\n## Cancellation\n\nPass an `abortSignal` to cancel an in-flight request:\n\n```typescript\nimport { decide, boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { typesafeDecider } from '@tanstack/ai-typesafe'\n\nconst controller = new AbortController()\nsetTimeout(() => controller.abort(), 5000)\n\nconst result = await decide({\n  adapter: typesafeDecider('jev-latest'),\n  state: 'Please refund the extra payment.',\n  questions: {\n    refund: boolean({\n      instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n    }),\n  },\n  abortSignal: controller.signal,\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.refund.value)\n```\n\n## Observability\n\nAttach observe-only middleware to track usage, completion, errors, and\ncancellation. This is the same `GenerationMiddleware` contract the media\nactivities use:\n\n```typescript\nimport { decide, boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { typesafeDecider } from '@tanstack/ai-typesafe'\n\nconst result = await decide({\n  adapter: typesafeDecider('jev-latest'),\n  state: 'Please refund the extra payment.',\n  questions: {\n    refund: boolean({\n      instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n    }),\n  },\n  middleware: [\n    {\n      name: 'usage-logger',\n      onUsage: (_ctx, usage) => {\n        console.log(`prompt tokens: ${usage.promptTokens}`)\n      },\n    },\n  ],\n})\n\nconsole.log(result.refund.value)\n```\n\n> **Tip:** Pass `otelMiddleware()` to emit OpenTelemetry spans for evaluate\n> calls. See [OpenTelemetry](../advanced/otel).\n\n## Environment Variables\n\nEach adapter reads its own key:\n\n- TypeSafe: `TYPESAFE_API_KEY`\n- OpenRouter: `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`\n- Vercel AI Gateway: `AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY` (or `VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN`)\n- Cloudflare REST: `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` and `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN`\n\nYou only need the key for the adapter you pick.\n\n## Error Handling\n\n```typescript\nimport { decide, boolean } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { typesafeDecider } from '@tanstack/ai-typesafe'\n\ntry {\n  const result = await decide({\n    adapter: typesafeDecider('jev-latest'),\n    state: 'Please refund the extra payment.',\n    questions: {\n      refund: boolean({\n        instructions: 'Is the customer asking for a refund?',\n      }),\n    },\n  })\n  console.log(result.refund.value)\n} catch (error) {\n  if (error instanceof Error) {\n    console.error('Evaluate failed:', error.message)\n  }\n}\n```\n\nIf `questions` is empty, `decide()` throws before any request.\nIf a question key is `meta`, `decide()` throws.\n\n## Runnable Example\n\n`examples/react/evaluate` is a small TanStack Start app that runs this page.\nPaste a support ticket. The UI shows queue, urgency, and refund.\nThe dropdown lists five adapters. Each call to `decide()` uses the same questions.\n\n1. Copy `.env.example` to `.env`.\n2. If you pick a hosted adapter, add its key in `.env`.\n3. If you pick Ollaya, run `ollaya serve`.\n4. If you pick Ollaya, run `ollaya pull laya:latest`.\n5. Run the dev server with the command below.\n\nOllaya does not need an API key.\n\n```bash\npnpm --filter evaluate dev\n```\n\nOpen http://localhost:3100.\n\n## Next Steps\n\nLocal:\n\n- [Ollaya Adapter](../adapters/ollaya) - Local `laya` decisions. No API key.\n- [TypeSafe Adapter](../adapters/typesafe) - Direct Jev, models, and explicit API keys\n- [Evaluate a ticket](../tutorials/evaluate) - Build a Start route that routes a ticket\n\nHosted:\n\n- [OpenRouter Adapter](../adapters/openrouter) - Evaluate through your OpenRouter key\n- [Vercel AI Gateway](../adapters/vercel-gateway) - Evaluate through the Gateway\n- [Cloudflare Adapter](../adapters/cloudflare) - Evaluate from a Worker or REST\n"}
